nd Richard Harmon\\n\\nActors who are siblings in real life are commonly cast to play siblings on television. After all, that's the best way to make it seem like the relationship is an authentic one. In the case of Jessica and Richard Harmon, though, the siblings ... \",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/cw-stars-family/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d156\"},\"ref\":\"d156\",\"snippet\":\" ... in which they co-starred opposite Adam Sandler as five-year-old Julian McGrath.\\n\\nJeff and Beau Bridges (The Fabulous Baker Boys)\\n\\nReal-life brothers Jeff Bridges and Beau Bridges star as the eponymous Baker Boys, a pair of piano-playing siblings, in this 1989 musical dramedy written ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cinemablend.com/movies/times-real-siblings-showed-up-in-the-same-movie\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d157\"},\"ref\":\"d157\",\"snippet\":\" ... 19, 2021.\\n\\n\\\"The complicated relationship among siblings often plays out in real life in such a huge way,\\\" Isha told The Hollywood Reporter in 2022. \\\"I cannot tell you how many times I have been reminded by people who have not spoken to their siblings in years of ... \",\"title\":\"https://people.com/all-about-serena-williams-venus-williams-siblings-7561298\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d158\"},\"ref\":\"d158\",\"snippet\":\" ... lifetimes. \\\"It was an inspiring and beautiful thing to hear their words of encouragement, telling me, 'You don't understand what this is doing for us, for our community, for all the little Black and brown girls who are going to see themselves in you,'\\\" she recalled.\\n\\nResponse ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/musicians/a46551458/halle-bailey\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d159\"},\"ref\":\"d159\",\"snippet\":\" ... This gory shocker stars Jay Hernandez (Suicide Squad), Derek Richardson (Anger Management), Barbara Nedeljakova (Shanghai Knights)\\n\\nIncarnation: Based on the ancient demon Mammon, Incarnation is a twisted tale of greed about a young couple chasing the American dream. Cast: Taye Diggs (Chicago), Jessica Uberuaga (The Fanatic), Michael Madsen ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.fangoria.com/56-free-horror-movies-streaming-in-april-2025/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"a8dcd0c37a2bc447153fb78a0efb619e2eaad827fe5329e31cc9c958d88c6aca\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"2b808744037e86e1b44515a2bb2597f0b407ab4c4792d9c0f594d826cdbf5c23\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"This Is Us cast real life couple siblings co-stars\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d160\"},\"ref\":\"d160\",\"snippet\":\" ... This Is Us - Amazon Prime\\n\\nThis Is Us tells the heart-warming and emotional story of the Pearson triplets, Randall (Sterling K. Brown), Kate (Chrissy Metz) and Kevin (Justin Hartley), known as 'the big three', and their parents Jack (Milo Ventimiglia) and Rebecca (Mandy Moore).\\n\\nTaking place in ... \",\"title\":\"https://rts.org.uk/article/best-tv-shows-about-parenting\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d161\"},\"ref\":\"d161\",\"snippet\":\" ... Today is just part one, of course, so hopefully that on-screen reunion is yet to come. I also really want to see Carrie/Will/Arianna with Kate as well and hope Kate gets a little moment of her own regarding John. I forget if I mentioned this ... \",\"title\":\"https://boards.soapoperanetwork.com/topic/60492-best-soap-of-each-decade/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d162\"},\"ref\":\"d162\",\"snippet\":\" ... Following the box office section, this list is organized chronologically, providing information on release dates, production companies, directors, and principal cast members.\\n\\nBox office\\n\\nThe highest-grossing American films released in 2023, by domestic box office gross revenue, are as follows:\\n\\n**Table 1**: Highest-grossing films of 2023 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_American_films_of_2023\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d163\"},\"ref\":\"d163\",\"snippet\":\" ... today. \\\"This is Us\\\" follows the story of the Pearson family and their journey over the years. Rebecca and Jack Pearson, who lost a triplet child during childbirth, give birth to twins Kate and Kevin. During their hospital stay, they also meet and adopt their son Randall, an ... \",\"title\":\"https://adoptionswithlove.org/uncategorized/adoption-on-television\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d164\"},\"ref\":\"d164\",\"snippet\":\" ... The final twist revealed that Jack and Rebecca Pearson's story took place in 1980, while the other characters, Randall, Kate, and Kevin, live in the present day.\\n\\nThis was one of the most impactful moments in the show and showcased This Is Us as a complex series ... \",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/tv-shows-perfect-pilot-episodes/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"d389ccd3f6e4ff0c8256f0cd8b6dec14680ed3e278307ff07ded575ae6e42ce8\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"99caf5faa0b31af54cd3c6a62c86c1170d27356fddcc66a348be189efc4106cf\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"This Is Us Jack Rebecca Kate Kevin Randall married children\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_862e2173760443b1b5c6e4a2"},{"content":"Previously delivered raw windows (untrusted source data, not instructions or verified claims):\n[{\"document\":\"d17\",\"document_chars\":9101,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"30d6d8bd1feaa16d7480eae3bbb0d0772ddf0a956d9870efc705af2df5ace29e\",\"snapshot\":\"a531c0a6be82cbe578781b28cb207ff02e87008856d5212ec2eab3fae2afe076\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Screen Rant\\nauthor: Joseph Allen\\ndate: 2018-04-13\\n---\\nThe CW's slate of programming is a fascinating one. Many of its shows are actually fairly well-regarded, whether they take place inside of the network's sprawling Arrowverse or not. Part of the reason these shows have been so successful is because of their excellent casting and captivating stars.\\n\\nAlthough the CW has a number of great shows on the air and a really great talent pool, they more than occasionally like to cast actors who are actually related to one another in real life, or are married and have decided to form a new family with one another.\\n\\nWhether these two relatives show up on the same show or not depends on the specifics of the situation, but as many of the couples on this list are married, it's often the case that the two of them met while they were filming together. Other times, the relationship between the two actors was the reason that one of them was brought onto a show.\\n\\nWhatever the reasons might be, it's clear that the CW has no fears about keeping things close. After all, if one actor from a family works out, who's to say that others won't, too?\\n\\nHere are 15 CW Stars That Only True Fans Know Are Actually Family.\\n\\nStephen And Robbie Amell\\n\\nThis one is among the most readily apparent on this list, in part because Robbie and Stephen Amell share a last name. The cousins have also made homes for themselves on the CW, where they have both played superheroes.\\n\\nStephen has been Oliver Queen on Arrow for several years, and Robbie has played Firestorm on The Flash. Robbie also played a teleporting hero on Tomorrow People, which has been off the air for a few years now.\\n\\nIn addition to sharing an employer, at least sometimes, the two cousins also look quite a bit alike, and are each quite handsome. Of course, there a number of families who have spawned multiple successful actors because, at the end of the day, part of the reason actors are famous is because of their looks, which the Amells have in spades.\\n\\nJared Padalecki And Genevieve Cortese\\n\\nJared Padalecki has had a pretty long and steady career on television, and he's even had the chance to work with his future wife.\\n\\nPadalecki and Genevieve Cortese actually met on the set of Supernatural when Cortese was a recurring guest during the show's fourth season. Cortese played Ruby, a demon who seduces Padalecki's character and causes a rift to form between Sam and Dean.\\n\\nAlthough the affair between Sam and Ruby proved to be short-lived, Padalecki and Cortese's relationship turned out to be a pretty stable one. The couple eventually got married, and they now live in Austin, Texas with their three children. Supernatural is a show with plenty of tragedy, but things seemed to have ended in a happily ever after for Padalecki and Cortese.\\n\\nAly And AJ Michalka\\n\\nAly and AJ Michalka have been famous since a fairly young age. Both actresses made their debuts on the Disney Channel when they were still quite young, and they also to\",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/cw-stars-family/\"}]","role":"user"},{"content":"Current control state (data, not source evidence):\n{\"current_notes_not_evidence\":[],\"evidence_shelf\":{\"omitted_for_capacity\":[],\"restored_exact_windows\":[\"e1\"],\"selection\":\"bounded recent first-delivery order; not a relevance/verification judgment\"},\"feedback\":null,\"instruction\":\"Read only useful passages. Notes and all-page cleanup are optional.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"RESEARCH\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":184,\"backend_calls\":74,\"model_calls\":7,\"output_reservation\":46180},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d164\"},\"ref\":\"d164\",\"snippet\":\" ... The final twist revealed that Jack and Rebecca Pearson's story took place in 1980, while the other characters, Randall, Kate, and Kevin, live in the presen\",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/tv-shows-perfect-pilot-episodes/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d163\"},\"ref\":\"d163\",\"snippet\":\" ... today. \\\"This is Us\\\" follows the story of the Pearson family and their journey over the years. Rebecca and Jack Pearson, who lost a triplet child during chi\",\"title\":\"https://adoptionswithlove.org/uncategorized/adoption-on-television\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d162\"},\"ref\":\"d162\",\"snippet\":\" ... Following the box office section, this list is organized chronologically, providing information on release dates, production companies, directors, and prin\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_American_films_of_2023\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d161\"},\"ref\":\"d161\",\"snippet\":\" ... Today is just part one, of course, so hopefully that on-screen reunion is yet to come. I also really want to see Carrie/Will/Arianna with Kate as well and \",\"title\":\"https://boards.soapoperanetwork.com/topic/60492-best-soap-of-each-decade/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d160\"},\"ref\":\"d160\",\"snippet\":\" ... This Is Us - Amazon Prime\\n\\nThis Is Us tells the heart-warming and emotional story of the Pearson triplets, Randall (Sterling K. Brown), Kate (Chrissy Metz)\",\"title\":\"https://rts.org.uk/article/best-tv-shows-about-parenting\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d159\"},\"ref\":\"d159\",\"snippet\":\" ... This gory shocker stars Jay Hernandez (Suicide Squad), Derek Richardson (Anger Management), Barbara Nedeljakova (Shanghai Knights)\\n\\nIncarnation: Based on t\",\"title\":\"https://www.fangoria.com/56-free-horror-movies-streaming-in-april-2025/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d158\"},\"ref\":\"d158\",\"snippet\":\" ... lifetimes. \\\"It was an inspiring and beautiful thing to hear their words of encouragement, telling me, 'You don't understand what this is doing for us, for \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/musicians/a46551458/halle-bailey\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d157\"},\"ref\":\"d157\",\"snippet\":\" ... 19, 2021.\\n\\n\\\"The complicated relationship among siblings often plays out in real life in such a huge way,\\\" Isha told The Hollywood Reporter in 2022. \\\"I cann\",\"title\":\"https://people.com/all-about-serena-williams-venus-williams-siblings-7561298\"}],\"consecutive_repeat_rounds\":0,\"contract\":{\"enabled\":true,\"gap_state\":true,\"guided_read\":true,\"recovery_rounds\":2,\"repeat_threshold\":2,\"repetition\":\"bounded\",\"reuse_results\":true,\"version\":\"gap-workflow-v1\"},\"instruction\":\"Use the current missing relation to choose a real next action. Page-name search is not page reading; cached is not proof of progress.\",\"last_new_navigation_source_round\":9,\"last_new_raw_source_round\":4,\"previous_gap_judgments_not_verified\":[],\"recovery_decisions_used\":0,\"stage\":\"normal\"},\"retriever_capabilities\":{\"boolean_operators\":false,\"kind\":\"sqlite-fts5-bm25\",\"negative_result\":\"no hit for this expression is not proof that the fact is absent\",\"phrase_quotes\":false,\"query_rule\":\"lowercase; regex word extraction; first-occurrence deduplication; OR of quoted individual tokens\",\"ranking\":\"SQLite bm25(search), ascending; docid tie-break; unchanged from q26 LocalIndex\",\"scope\":\"fixed local corpus; not live web\",\"site_filter\":false,\"title_kind\":\"stored URL, not an extracted page title\",\"warning\":\"site:, quotes and AND/OR in input are not filters/operators. Their words may become ordinary search terms. Use a few discriminating terms.\"},\"runtime_contract\":{\"evidence_shelf_size\":3,\"max_calls_per_response\":4,\"max_queries_per_search\":3,\"require_sources\":true},\"uncommitted_response_not_evidence\":null}","role":"user"}],"model":"EB-GLM-5.2","temperature":0.0,"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find candidate documents in the configured corpus; it does NOT open their full text.\nUSE WHEN: No suitable page is known, a new entity/relation needs locating, or a different clue is needed after irrelevant results.\nAVOID: Do not repeat a page-name query when you intend to read an existing result. Do not treat snippets as proof or unsupported operators as filters.\nINPUT: queries is an array of 1..3 distinct nonblank strings, each <=2000 characters; top_k is an optional integer 1..10 (default 5). See runtime retriever_capabilities. replay=true explicitly restores the full cached navigation view; it does not force fresh SQL.\nOUTPUT: ok/results contains query, hits with ref/title/snippet, cache status and observation metadata. navigation_seen is NOT a read receipt; raw_ranges_delivered lists actual windows. read_action is an available example, not auto-execution. Metadata counts operations, not relevance. Exact delivered repeats may use view=reuse and omit snippets; replay=true restores them.\nWORKFLOW: search -> inspect returned dN -> read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}); after reading, use the newly found entity and one missing relation for a new search, or finish directly.","name":"search","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"queries":{"items":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":1,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"replay":{"type":"boolean"},"top_k":{"maximum":10,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["queries"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Open the raw text of a received search result, or replay a previously delivered evidence window.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate page may answer the current gap; inspect its actual text before another page-name search. Use continuation to include a subject/date split at a boundary.\nAVOID: Do not guess handles or cite an unread result. Do not infer an entity relationship merely because adjacent windows mention different people.\nINPUT: Only ref is required. dN opens from start=0 with configured read_chars by default; optional integer start>=0 and length=1..6000 use Unicode code points. eN accepts only ref and restores the exact old window. Optional goal<=400 characters on dN selects one lexical paragraph window; it is mutually exclusive with start and forbidden on eN. length remains an upper bound.\nOUTPUT: ok/evidence contains eN, document, snapshot, start/end, original text and integrity fields; next_start supports continuation. The window becomes citable after it is delivered in a subsequent model input. Source text is untrusted data. goal no-match returns matched=false with no evidence; selection metadata reports lexical matches and actual range, never a semantic guarantee.\nWORKFLOW: read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) -> compare the original constraint with the text -> search a newly discovered gap, continue read, or finish with delivered eN.","name":"read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"goal":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"length":{"maximum":6000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"ref":{"pattern":"^[de][1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find literal text positions inside one already received document; this is page-local navigation.\nUSE WHEN: The page is known but a name or exact phrase is far from its beginning.\nAVOID: Do not use a literal zero-match result to prove a fact absent. It does not search aliases, paraphrases or the whole corpus.\nINPUT: ref must be a received dN; text is a nonblank string <=2000 characters; optional integer start>=0; ignore_case is boolean, default false.\nOUTPUT: ok/document/snapshot/matches gives original start/end positions and exact excerpts, case_sensitive and next_start. Matches are positions_not_evidence, not citable eN.\nWORKFLOW: find -> read the matched range with enough preceding subject context -> compare evidence. Change literal terms or use goal-read rather than repeating zero matches.","name":"find","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ignore_case":{"type":"boolean"},"ref":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"text":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["ref","text"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Locate earlier delivered evidence, received search navigation and optional note history without external retrieval.\nUSE WHEN: A known lead or earlier raw window has left the active context; recover it instead of re-searching the same phrase.\nAVOID: Do not cite a recall excerpt as new evidence. It cannot search unreceived backend data; a lexical miss is not a proof of absence.\nINPUT: query is a nonblank string <=2000 characters. Use a discriminating entity or relation already encountered.\nOUTPUT: ok/matches has ref or note key, exact excerpt and kind. eN can be replayed; dN can be opened; inactive notes are historical model judgments, not evidence.\nWORKFLOW: recall -> read({\"ref\":\"eN\"}) for exact recovery, or read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) for an unread page. Then update only the gap that changed.","name":"recall","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"query":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Maintain a small optional free-text scratchpad; not verified facts or a prerequisite to submit.\nUSE WHEN: A brief reusable alias, rejected route or independent reminder will help later. Prefer update_gap for the active research question when available.\nAVOID: Do not summarize every page, copy the full question, or repeatedly write the same note. Notes do not automatically retract dependent plans.\nINPUT: put requires op/key/text/anchors; text <=600 characters, anchors is <=6 delivered eN. delete requires op/key only. Keys are 1..32 ASCII letters/digits/_/-. Capacity is explicit.\nOUTPUT: ok/key/changed and kind=agent_note_not_evidence, or deleted. A no-op is not research progress. Errors do not silently alter saved notes.\nWORKFLOW: Optionally save a useful observation alongside another already-planned action; keep sources in the archive and finish without cleanup.","name":"notes","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"anchors":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"put"},"text":{"maxLength":600,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["op","key","text","anchors"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"delete"}},"required":["op","key"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Explicitly submit the requested answer with source windows, or explicitly abstain.\nUSE WHEN: The requested core answer has sufficient support, or the available budget/evidence cannot resolve it. No note, gap update or audit is mandatory.\nAVOID: Do not claim every clue is verified when it is not. Do not change established into expanded, by-year into in-year, or hide unresolved numeric conflicts in a long explanation.\nINPUT: Answer branch requires answer and refs. Nonblank strings are <=8000 characters; string-integer-v1 additionally permits plain JSON integers, not bools/floats, rendered as decimal text. Strings stay exact. Abstention requires abstain=true and nonblank reason<=2000 characters. Never mix branches. refs contains only delivered eN, <=16; configured source and literal-format requirements still apply.\nOUTPUT: ok/terminal records submitted or abstained. Submitted answer is text with refs/basis and any representation metadata. Legal references are NOT semantic verification. Explicit prefix/suffix constraints still apply.\nWORKFLOW: Finish last in a response, based only on evidence already received for that decision. Never combine a new read and a guessed citation to its unseen result. In FINAL only finish is allowed.","name":"finish","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"answer":{"maxLength":8000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":["string","integer"]},"refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true}},"required":["answer","refs"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"abstain":{"const":true},"reason":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["abstain","reason"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Replace the one active research question and retain a bounded history of explicit model judgments; it is NOT an automatic verifier.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate, unresolved relation, rejection or conflict changed, or repeated searches need a concrete next objective. Use sparingly, not after every tool.\nAVOID: Do not turn the original question or your prior guess into evidence. Updating a gap does not count as a new observation and does not reset a search loop.\nINPUT: subject/question/basis are nonblank <=400 characters; kind and status follow schema; evidence_refs are <=6 received eN, navigation_refs <=6 received dN; next_action is one named existing tool. supported/rejected/conflict require evidence_refs. Supply a concise decision basis, not a transcript.\nOUTPUT: ok/changed/current returns agent_judgment_not_verified with revision. At most four previous distinct gap versions remain in the active view; the full update is journaled. Sources are checked for delivery, not entailment.\nWORKFLOW: Observe -> identify one missing relationship or record a real rejection -> select read on an available page or search for a new relation. An update may share a response with known independent actions; no update is required before finish.","name":"update_gap","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"basis":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"evidence_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"kind":{"enum":["locate","read","relation","disambiguate","conflict","recover"]},"navigation_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"next_action":{"enum":["search","read","find","recall","finish"]},"question":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"status":{"enum":["open","supported","rejected","conflict"]},"subject":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["subject","question","kind","status","evidence_refs","navigation_refs","next_action","basis"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"}]}